{
  "id": "musique_actuelle",
  "name": "Musique actuelle (Montreal creative music)",
  "family": "jazz",
  "lineage": "Montreal-centred current of composed and improvised music that took the name musique actuelle in the early 1980s, when the Ambiances Magnetiques label, run by a collective of Montreal musicians, and the Festival International de Musique Actuelle de Victoriaville (FIMAV), both founded in 1983, gave it a label and a stage. Its musicians, among them guitarist Rene Lussier and saxophonist and flutist Jean Derome, combine free improvisation, rock, jazz, Quebec folk song, noise and contemporary composition, with a taste for collage, humour and the French language.",
  "recipe": "classic 1980-1983 musique actuelle, improv On Frame, jam free branch. group vocals. single coil electric guitar, selmer mark vi canonical 1954 1974 jazz paris continuous-airflow legato saxophone, flute, electric bass, bronze bell bronze machine hammered symmetric pattern organized rows drum kit. live tracking. tube condenser, 500-series boutique pre, brick-wall limiter, dynamic EQ. 24-bit digital plate reverb digital delay pitch shifter.",
